.SH NAME
lmm-service-status - Show whether lmm-serve.service is installed, enabled and running


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm service status [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show whether lmm-serve.service is installed (and by whom), enabled and
running, the unit file systemd uses, and whether lingering is on - that is,
whether your user services start at boot rather than at login.

.PP
Examples:
  lmm service status
  lmm service status --json


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for status


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lmm or ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: $XDG_DATA_HOME/lmm or ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output JSON instead of text; mutating commands print their result, --dry-run prints the plan; never prompts

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="off"
	diagnostic log level written to stderr (off, error, warn, info, debug)

.PP
